      <div type="clause" n="36.5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ECfRetr">ECf retr</ref> 36.5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="ECf retr 36.5"><pb n="667" ed="#liebermann"/><hi rend="bold">Deinde</hi> iusticia episcopi faciat uenire processionem cum sacerdote induto alba <hi rend="bold">et manipulo</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="g" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.fn.g"/> et stola et clericis in superpelliciis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.26"/> cum aqua benedicta et cruce, <hi rend="bold">precedentibus</hi> candelabris et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.27"/> thuribulo cum igne et incenso; et <hi rend="bold">amici</hi> extrahant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.28"/> mortuum, <hi rend="spaced">deponentes</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.29"/> in feretrum, <hi rend="spaced">portantes</hi> eum ad ecclesiam; <hi rend="bold">ibi</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.30"/> missa <hi rend="bold">pro</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.31"/> <hi rend="bold">defuncto celebrata,</hi> et <hi rend="bold">cetero</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.32"/> <hi rend="bold">peracto officio</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.33"/>, interrent eum, <hi rend="bold">ut decet</hi> Christianum. Ab ipso <hi rend="bold">uero</hi> die in XVI<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.34"/> diebus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.35"/> reddat <hi rend="bold">interfector</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.36"/> episcopo tres forisfacturas: unam quia legalem pro<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.37"/> latrone interfecit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.38"/>; alteram<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.39"/> quia fratrem suum pro<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.40"/> <pb n="668" ed="#liebermann"/>latrone interrauit, quod Angli dicunt his emcristene<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.1"/>; tertiam <hi rend="bold">eo</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.2"/> <hi rend="bold">quod</hi> uadimonium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.3"/> dedit ad dirationandum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.4"/> se, et non potuit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.5"/>.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="667"><label>printed alongside</label> <ref target="clause:ECf_36-5">ECf 36.5</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 667–668 (November 2026): read from the page images and checked against the scan’s own text layer, differences settled against the page; the words in bold are the Retractator’s changes to ECf, as Liebermann prints them.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.fn.g" n="g" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">der Zusatz des Retr. ist nicht jünger: den Manipel trug der Priester längst; Braun</hi> Priesterl. Gewänder 55. 75</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the Retr.’s addition is not later: the priest had long worn the maniple; Braun, Priesterl. Gewänder 55. 75</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.fn.h" n="h" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vom</hi> sterquilinium in cimiterium <hi rend="italic">ward ein nach dem Tode unschuldig Befundener</hi> 1259 <hi rend="italic">übertragen;</hi> Math. Paris. V 739</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in 1259 a man found innocent after his death was moved from the sterquilinium into the cimiterium; Math. Paris. V 739</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.fn.i" n="i" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Strafgeld hierfür gehört doch dem weltlichen Gerichtsherrn; dazu kommen Wergeld an die Sippe und Mannbusse an den Herrn des Erschlagenen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">yet the fine for this belongs to the secular lord of the court; in addition there are the wergeld to the kin and the manbot to the lord of the slain man</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.fn.a-p668" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">668</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nebenchristen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fellow Christians</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-pelitiis <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> suppel. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-pelitiis Cb; suppel. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cum t. et i. <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cum t. et i. Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">extrahentes m. ponant <hi rend="italic">Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">extrahentes m. ponant Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">deferentes <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">deferentes Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ubi <hi rend="italic">Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ubi Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. d. <hi rend="italic">übergeschr. Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. d. written above the line Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">alio o. p. <hi rend="italic">Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">alio o. p. Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">seruicio</hi> <hi rend="italic">Db</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">seruicio Db</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quindecim <hi rend="italic">Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quindecim Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.35" n="35" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dies <hi rend="italic">Va Hv K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dies Va Hv K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.36" n="36" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">illius <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hv adds illius</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.37" n="37" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">int. pro la. <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">int. pro la. Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.38" n="38" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-cerit <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-cerit K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.39" n="39" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aliam <hi rend="italic">Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">aliam Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.40" n="40" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. l. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. l. lacking in Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Cb Co;</hi> emcristine <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> euin(eunic. <hi rend="italic">Va</hi>)cr. <hi rend="italic">Lb Va;</hi> euencristen <hi rend="italic">Hv;</hi> enenec. <hi rend="italic">Db</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so Cb Co; emcristine K; euin(eunic. Va)cr. Lb Va; euencristen Hv; enenec. Db</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uadium <hi rend="italic">Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uadium Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">disra. <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">disra. Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.la.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">667</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt c.</hi> 15 <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. 15 follows in Lond</seg></note>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude-crib" ana="#fromLatin">Then let the bishop's justice cause a procession to come, with a priest vested in alb and maniple and stole and clerics in surplices, with holy water and cross, with candlesticks and censer with fire and incense going before; and let the friends draw out the dead man, laying [him] on a bier, carrying him to the church; there, when mass for the dead has been celebrated and the rest of the office performed, let them bury him, as befits a Christian. And from that day within sixteen days let the slayer pay to the bishop three forfeitures: one because he killed a lawful man as a thief; the second because he buried his brother as a thief, [the brother] whom the English call <hi rend="italic">his emcristene</hi> (his fellow-Christian); the third because he gave a gage to deraign himself (prove his case), and could not.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_36-5.lnote.oe.erkl-rs" n="Rs" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> II 60 Sp. 2 Z. 4 v. u. Zitierte druckte jetzt Förster <hi rend="italic">Festschr. für Morsbach</hi> 148. 164. — <hi rend="italic">interfecerit</hi><hi rend="superscript">38</hi> <hi rend="italic">emxpenne</hi><hi rend="superscript">1</hi> [<hi rend="italic">xp</hi> = <hi rend="italic">christ</hi>] — <hi rend="italic">disr.</hi><hi rend="superscript">4</hi> — <hi rend="italic">potuit</hi><hi rend="superscript">5</hi>; folgt c. 15 Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">What is cited above, II 60 col. 2 l. 4 from bottom, has now been printed by Förster <hi rend="italic">Festschr. für Morsbach</hi> 148. 164. — <hi rend="italic">interfecerit</hi><hi rend="superscript">38</hi> <hi rend="italic">emxpenne</hi><hi rend="superscript">1</hi> [<hi rend="italic">xp</hi> = <hi rend="italic">christ</hi>] — <hi rend="italic">disr.</hi><hi rend="superscript">4</hi> — <hi rend="italic">potuit</hi><hi rend="superscript">5</hi>; c. 15 follows, Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
